ons to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback, the service is healthy on v2.3.0 in every region and the error rate is 0.2%. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before trying to deploy it again.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "confidence": 0.93}, "confidence": 0.93}, {"t_ms": 16490, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01U4RbLBWHjkiRg4uqADQ6hP", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 16490, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01U4RbLBWHjkiRg4uqADQ6hP", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 19944, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened incident INC-0001 as a SEV2.\n\n- **What was wrong:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west, failing health checks with an 18% error rate. Its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had also failed in staging.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release marked healthy in production. All three regions now run it, health checks pass, and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 describes the failure and the rollback, and recommends finding the root cause before v2.3.1 is deployed again. Opening it paged the on-call engineer.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01E24Xuhtix4JTBoKz7GvEVY", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_011ZoJk3y7ATGddHu4CEdYSs", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input"